WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:04.890
If you've seen The Lego Batman Movie, you'll
know it includes not only super-well-known

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.291
villains like the Joker, but also an incredible
range of other villains from the DC Comics

00:00:09.291 --> 00:00:10.769
rogues gallery.

00:00:10.769 --> 00:00:14.209
And scattered throughout the movie, there
are also some cool voice cameos you might

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:15.230
not have taken in.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:19.070
So, in this video, I'm gonna run through many
of those villains and cameos for you.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:22.570
Quick warning, there are spoilers ahead, so
if you're not ready for those, get out of

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:27.590
Gotham by tapping or clicking here to watch
my spoiler-free LEGO Batman Movie review.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:31.690
By the way, I'll have a great giveaway to
win a pair of awesome Lego Batman Movie books

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:37.219
on my Lego Batman easter egg video, so make
sure you subscribe and turn on your notifications

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:38.469
so you don't miss out!

00:00:38.469 --> 00:00:42.629
Ok, let's start with the villains that the
Joker hires for his dastardly attack on the

00:00:42.629 --> 00:00:45.670
Gotham Energy Facility at the beginning of
the movie.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.559
The first celebrity cameo is by talk show
host Conan O'Brien who voices The Riddler,

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:53.850
and he's joined by Scarecrow who masquerades
as a pizza delivery guy and is voiced by comic

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.969
actor Jason Mantzoukas.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:00.339
Doug Benson voices Bane and does a good job
sounding very similar to Tom Hardy's take

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:02.979
on the character in The Dark Knight Rises.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:06.960
Classic Batman villain Two-Face is played
by Billy Dee Williams, who voiced his iconic

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.250
Star Wars character Lando Calrissian in the
first Lego Movie and he also played Harvey

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.810
Dent in the 1989 Batman movie.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:18.750
In fact, Williams had hoped Harvey Dent would
become Two-Face in the sequel Batman Returns,

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.620
but the character was dropped from that movie,
and when Two-Face did appear in Batman Forever,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:25.750
he was played by Tommy Lee Jones.

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:30.190
Catwoman, who helps the villains hack in to
the system, is voiced by Zoe Kravitz, who's

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:33.049
starred in X-Men: First Class and the Divergent
series.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:37.869
Indeed, Kravitz actually has some shocking
prior history with the Batman franchise, specifically

00:01:37.869 --> 00:01:41.870
The Dark Knight Rises, which she was informed
she couldn't audition for a small part in

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:46.130
because, to quote what she was told, "they
weren't 'going urban'".

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:51.170
The comedy-folk duo Garfunkel and Oates each
voice a villain in the movie, with Riki Lindhome

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:54.500
as Poison Ivy and Kate Micucci as Clayface.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:59.189
And rounding out The Joker's posse of major
villains is Harley Quinn voiced by Jenny Slate,

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:04.119
who was also the voice of Bellwether in Zootopia
and Gidget in The Secret Life of Pets.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:08.399
The Lego Batman Movie also pays homage to
an enormous stack of villains from Batman's

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:09.399
Rogues Gallery.

00:02:09.399 --> 00:02:13.590
Some are more familiar, like Penguin, who
turns up in a Lego version of his duck car

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:18.510
that we saw on screen in Batman Returns; there's
also Killer Croc, who we last aw in the Suicide

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.159
Squad movie, who exclaims "I did something"
when he switches on the bomb here; and there's

00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:27.190
Mr Freeze who has a touch of Arnold Schwarzenegger
from Batman and Robin about him when he says

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:28.879
"no, you freeze".

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:32.370
Red Hood also turns up in a blink-and-you'll-miss-him
moment during a fight scene.

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:36.980
The official Lego site describes this Red
Hood as a "mysterious super-villain" and adds

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.790
that "rumors suggest that [he] may have a
secret connection to Batman or one of his

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:41.980
arch-villains."

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.629
In the comics, Red Hood is an alias that has
been used by different characters, two significant

00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:49.300
ones being the Joker and Jason Todd.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.760
The Lego Jason Todd version of Red Hood has
already appeared in the Lego video games with

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.069
a drastically different look to this Red Hood
in the Lego Batman movie.

00:02:57.069 --> 00:03:01.860
And, the helmet, cape and bow-tie worn by
the Red Hood that appears in The Lego Batman

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:06.129
Movie suggest that this is the Joker Red Hood
rather than Jason Todd.

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:11.349
In the comics, Red Hood was also an alias
the Joker used for his criminal activities

00:03:11.349 --> 00:03:12.860
before he became the Joker.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:18.800
Other villains who appear on screen very briefly
include Captain Boomerang, aka Digger, who

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.220
gets kicked in the head by Batman in the movie.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.140
In the comics, he's a criminal who uses high-tech
boomerangs, and we last saw him on the big

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:28.459
screen played by Jai Courtney in the Suicide
Squad movie.

00:03:28.459 --> 00:03:34.550
There's also Man-Bat, who first appeared in
the comics in 1970 as Kirk Langstrom, a scientist

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:37.439
who accidentally turns himself into a bat.

00:03:37.439 --> 00:03:42.019
Man-Bat hasn't appeared yet in a live-action
Batman film despite being considered for various

00:03:42.019 --> 00:03:43.700
cancelled Batman projects.

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.490
The closest thing so far has been the bat
creature that attacked Bruce Wayne during

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.020
his nightmare in Batman V Superman.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.050
Perhaps one of the daftest villains in The
Lego Batman Movie, although frankly that's

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:56.129
a tough call, is Condiment King.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:04:00.610
He first appeared in Batman: The Animated
Series and has often been used for comedic

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:04.159
effect, with an emphasis on condiment-inspired
puns.

00:04:04.159 --> 00:04:08.530
The character was later introduced into the
comics under the name of Mitchell Mayo.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:13.900
King Tut is a Batman villain that was initially
created for the 1960s Batman TV series, and

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:16.250
was later adapted in the comic books.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:21.840
King Tut, aka William McElroy, was an Egyptologist
at Yale who transformed into a delusional

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.870
villain when he lost his mind after being
hit on the head during a student riot.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:30.550
Egghead, who turns ups in The Lego Batman
Movie egging the bat signal, is another villain

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:36.090
who appeared in the 1960s Batman TV series,
where he was played by Vincent Price.

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:41.050
Killer Moth first appeared in Batman issue
63 where he set himself up as the opposite

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.020
of Batman, helping Gotham's criminal underworld.

00:04:44.020 --> 00:04:49.000
Killer Moth also had a fake identity as a
rich guy called Cameron van Cleer and, similar

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.110
to Batman, he had a Mothmobile as well as
a Moth-signal that criminals used to call

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:54.110
him.

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:58.400
Kite-Man, aka Charles Brown in the comics,
is said to be partly inspired by the Peanuts

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.620
character Charlie Brown who struggled to fly
a kite.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:07.050
Kite-Man first appeared in 1960 in Batman
issue 133, and, as you can guess, he uses

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.650
kite-based weapons to fight Batman.

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:13.889
Gentleman Ghost is a supernatural villain
in the comics who was created when the thief

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:17.150
Jim Craddock was hanged by the gunfighter
Nighthawk.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.120
Polka-Dot Man is a Batman villain who, in
the comics, can transform the coloured dots

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.110
on his tricked-out costume into various weapons.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:29.130
Catman first appeared in Detective Comics
in 1963 and modelled his look on a combo of

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.020
Batman and Catwoman.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:36.319
March Harriet is based on the comic-book villain
Harriet Pratt, aka March Hare, who along with

00:05:36.319 --> 00:05:40.030
Tweedledum, Tweedledee, and the Mad Hatter
was part of the Wonderland Gang.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:44.190
The villainous Zebra Man has appeared in several
different versions in the comics.

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:48.449
In his first incarnation, he invented a machine
that charged his body with energy, which gave

00:05:48.449 --> 00:05:49.990
him his powers and stripes.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:55.160
He also wore a special belt to control his
body's powerful diamagnetic force.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.449
The Eraser is a villain whose costume includes
a mask with a giant eraser on top.

00:05:59.449 --> 00:06:04.380
And, suitably enough, he hires himself out
to criminals to erase evidence left at crime

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.380
scenes.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:10.710
Orca is the scientist Dr Grace Balin who experimented
with spinal cord regeneration after she was

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:11.710
paralysed.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:16.419
She transformed into an orca-human hybrid
after experimenting with orca tissue.

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:21.509
The comic-book version of Tarantula who appears
in the movie is the former FBI agent Catalina

00:06:21.509 --> 00:06:27.180
Flores, who takes the law into her own hands
to deal with corrupt police officers and criminals.

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:31.479
Clock King is a foe of Green Arrow in the
comics and used his clock and time-based skills

00:06:31.479 --> 00:06:36.319
to turn to crime as a way to support his sister
when he was mistakenly diagnosed with a terminal

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:37.400
illness.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:41.760
And Calendar Man is a date-obsessed villain
whose crimes relate to specific dates and

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:42.760
holidays.

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:47.039
Now, the Lego Batman Movie doesn't restrict
itself to villains from DC Comics, TV shows

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.039
or movies.

00:06:48.039 --> 00:06:52.569
In fact, the Phantom Zone is home to a number
of trapped non-DC villains.

00:06:52.569 --> 00:06:56.699
Comedian Eddie Izzard provides the voice of
Voldemort delivering some great lines like

00:06:56.699 --> 00:07:01.000
"stop moving around, muggles", and he also
uses the levitation charm "Wingardium Leviosa"

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.550
several times in the movie.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:06.639
I wonder what Ralph Fiennes, who plays Alfred
in this film and brought Voldemort to life

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:10.199
in the Harry Potter movies, thought of Eddie
Izzard's take on the character!

00:07:10.199 --> 00:07:14.650
Jemaine Clement, who you'll have heard recently
as the rather shiny crab Tamatoa in Moana,

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:18.610
delivers a comedic animated version of Sauron
from The Lord of the Rings.

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:22.540
The iconic ape King Kong also appears and
is voiced by Seth Green.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:27.229
Ellie Kemper, who you might know as The Unbreakable
Kimmy Schmidt or as Erin from The Office,

00:07:27.229 --> 00:07:31.000
lends her voice to Phyllis, the brightly coloured
brick who serves as the gatekeeper to the

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:32.000
Phantom Zone.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.509
There's also a bunch of other cool villains
including Doctor Who's Daleks, a velociraptor from

00:07:36.509 --> 00:07:42.759
Jurassic Park, Jaws, Medusa, the Gremlins,
Dracula, Agent Smith from The Matrix, and

00:07:42.759 --> 00:07:46.220
the Wicked Witch of the West also makes an
appearance with her flying monkeys.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:51.050
The hilarious Justice League anniversary party
scene also brings back some characters and

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.830
voices from the first Lego Movie.

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:57.460
Channing Tatum returns as the voice of Superman,
and Jonah Hill and Adam Devine are back as

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.070
Green Lantern and The Flash respectively.

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:04.569
Other Justice League members at the party
include Wonder Woman, Aquaman, Cyborg, Martian

00:08:04.569 --> 00:08:10.420
Manhunter who jokingly dubs himself Martian
Dancehunter, Green Arrow, Black Canary, Hawkman

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:16.130
&amp; Hawkgirl, the Wonder Twins &amp; Gleek, Black
Vulcan, Apache Chief, El Dorado, and Wonder

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.130
Dog.

00:08:17.130 --> 00:08:20.240
And in Gotham city, there are a few more celebrity
cameos.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:24.950
Singer Mariah Carey is the voice of Mayor
McCaskill, the retiring Commissioner Jim Gordon

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:29.770
is played by Pretty Woman's Hector Elizondo,
Chris Hardwick of Nerdist fame is one of the

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:34.410
reporters quizzing Barbara Gordon after the
Joker surrenders, and The Lego Batman Movie

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:39.360
director Chris McKay is Pilot Bill who argues
with the Joker about why Batman will foil

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:40.740
his evil plans.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.701
Now, did you have a favourite cameo in the
movie?

00:08:43.701 --> 00:08:47.830
And if there's a Lego Batman sequel, who would
you like to see have more screen time?

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:49.720
Let me know in the comments below.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:53.470
And if you enjoyed this, I really appreciate
if you hit that thumbs up button, share and

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:54.470
subscribe.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:58.210
You can also tap or click here for more of
my videos including all the best easter eggs

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.730
from The Lego Batman Movie.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.550
Thanks for watching and see you next time!

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:02.570
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers!

